	After playing I don't know how many games (of nearly every type
	of character), I finally had one that made it to 6th level...
	but he had a flaw - he got hungry.  So he prayed to his god,
	who got angry (why???) and dropped him to 5th level.  He
	managed to make to back to 6th level, had all his hit points
	and got hungry again.  So he killed a hobbit, and ate it 
	immediately...World spins, goes dark, and he dies of food
	poisoning.  Isn't this a little ridiculous?  I know there's
	supposed to be an element of luck involved in the game,
	but when you've been extremely careful you should be rewarded,
	not killed!  The character never even had a chance.  Why isn't
	there some way to tell if something's tainted before you've
	eatten so much of it that you die from rotten food? (By the way,
	this was a Barbarian, so the food wasn't poisoned...he could
	have handled that)

	Also, has anyone looked at the code that determines the length 
	of blindness and hallucination?  They last an extraordinary
	length of time as compared things you like to have happen to
	you (like invisibility).

	For reference, we're using 3.0 patch level 3f (we removed the
	two calls to set_omask in pickup.c that got left around by the
	level 3 patches) on a Sun running 3.5/4.0

